<title>ITALY: SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in Italian first</p>
<p>division after matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>12 - Filippo Inzaghi (Atalanta)</p>
<p>11 - Abel Balbo (Roma), Vincenzo Montella (Sampdoria)</p>
<p>10 - Roberto Mancini (Sampdoria), Marcello Otero (Vicenza)</p>
<p>8 - Gabriel Batistuta (Fiorentina), Youri Djorkaeff (Inter),</p>
<p>Pasquale Luiso (Piacenza)</p>
<p>7 - Giuseppe Signori (Lazio), George Weah (Milan)</p>
<p>6 - Oliver Bierhoff and Paolo Poggi (both Udinese), Enrico</p>
<p>Chiesa (Parma), Igor Kolyvanov (Bologna), Luis Oliveira</p>
<p>(Fiorentina), Michele Padovano (Juventus), Sandro Tovalieri</p>
<p>(Cagliari)</p>
<p>5 - Alfredo Aglietti and Nicola Caccia (both Napoli),</p>
<p>Alessandro Del Piero (Juventus), Filippo Maniero (Verona),</p>
<p>Anselmo Robbiati (Fiorentina)</p>
<p>4 - Demetrio Albertini, Roberto Baggio and Christophe Dugarry</p>
<p>(all Milan), Marcio Amoroso (Udinese), Marco Branca and Marco</p>
<p>Delvecchio (both Inter), Marco Carparelli (Sampdoria), Andrea</p>
<p>Cruz (Napoli), Carmine Gautieri and Marco Negri (both Perugia),</p>
<p>Giampiero Maini and Roberto Murgita (both Vicenza),  Roberto</p>
<p>Muzzi (Cagliari)</p>
</text>
